<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= typeof lang !== 'undefined' ? lang : 'en' %>" dir="<%= typeof dir !== 'undefined' ? dir : 'ltr' %>">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Privacy Policy — Evo Meals' }) %>
<meta name="description" content="How Evo Meals collects, uses, shares, and retains data from parents, students, schools, and catering partners.">
</head>
<body>

<%- include('partials/sitenav', { active: '' }) %>

<section class="hero hero-inner-page">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="hero-copy" data-reveal style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated 19 September 2026. This explains what we collect, why, who it's shared with, and how long we keep it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap legal-content">
    <div class="faq-list">

      <div class="faq-item is-open">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="true"><span>Personal Contact Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We may collect information including your first and last name, Civil ID number, school information, your child's name and student details, contact numbers, and email address (together, "Personally Identifiable Information" or PII). We may also collect information about your past orders, service questions, reviews, and preferences — like meal types you tend to choose.</p>
          <p>We separately collect Non-Personally Identifiable Information — aggregated and demographic data that doesn't reveal who you specifically are — and IP address information, which is automatically logged by our servers whenever you visit the site, along with the time and pages visited.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Your Email Address &amp; Contact Number</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>To register, we'll need your email address and other contact details so we can reach you. We use these to confirm your order and get in touch if there's an issue with it — an email address is required to register. You can access, update, or correct this information any time through your account. If you'd rather not provide an email address, that's your choice, but you won't be able to register or place orders without one.</p>
          <p>We share part of your contact information — your name and your child's and school's details — with the catering partner preparing and delivering the meal. We also use this information to support and improve your experience on the site, to communicate with you, for our internal purposes, and to meet any legal requirements. It may be shared with our staff and with third parties directly involved in delivering your order or supporting your use of the site.</p>
          <p>We don't sell your personal contact information, and we won't share it with third parties beyond what's described here without your permission — unless we're legally required to, for example by court order, or to help prevent fraud or another crime.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Payment Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>When you place an order, you'll choose a payment method. We're not interested in your card details and we don't store your debit or credit card information ourselves.</p>
          <p>Online card payment is currently the only payment method available. Card transactions are transmitted to the relevant card company in encrypted form, following globally accepted security standards.</p>
          <p>If you choose to, we may keep part of your card information in encrypted form, with physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards in place to protect it.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Order Placement Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>Placing an order requires information like your name, your child's and school's details, phone number, and email address — what's needed to identify who the meal is for and complete the order. This information is shared with the catering partner as part of processing your order, under an agreement that restricts how they can use or share it. We'll use it to keep you updated on your order status. We won't share it with other business partners or affiliates without your permission, and it's treated as confidential unless we're required by law to disclose it.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Navigation &amp; Click Stream Data</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>As you browse, we collect data on which pages you visit, which features you use, and how long you spend on a page. This doesn't reveal your identity or get linked to you personally. We use it to support and improve your experience, complete your orders, meet legal requirements, and — where relevant — to show more useful content or recommendations, on our site or elsewhere. This data may be shared with our staff and with third parties directly supporting your order or your use of the site.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Marketing</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We don't sell or rent your personal information to third parties for their own marketing without your clear consent. We may combine information we hold with information from other companies to improve and personalize our service, content, and advertising.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Do We Disclose Your Personal Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We may share your information with our staff and with third parties involved in delivering your order or supporting your use of the site. We may also disclose it where necessary to protect our legal rights, in connection with actual or suspected harmful conduct, or in good faith where we believe it's needed to meet a legal requirement or court order, or to protect our property, our users, or the public — including sharing information with other organizations for fraud or credit-risk prevention.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How Is Personally Identifiable Information Disclosed?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We may share PII: with service providers who support things like hosting, data analysis, payment processing, order fulfillment, infrastructure, IT, customer service, email delivery, and card processing, so they can provide those services to us; with our catering partners so they can fulfil your order; with anyone you message through the site regarding site-related content; under the terms of any applicable service rules where they govern how your PII is treated; and with a successor organization in the event of a merger, sale, or similar change to our business.</p>
          <p>We may also disclose it where we believe appropriate — under applicable law (including outside your country of residence), to comply with legal process, to respond to public or government authority requests, to enforce our terms, to protect our or our affiliates' operations, to protect rights, privacy, safety, or property, or to pursue available legal remedies.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Cookies</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>When you visit our site, our server sends a small file called a cookie to your device, which helps identify you as a returning user and saves you time by remembering your details. Cookies can't carry viruses and can only be read by the server that sent them. You can accept or decline cookies through your browser settings — though some site features may not work fully if cookies are disabled.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Protection of Your Personal Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>Our site uses secure pages to collect your information, and we store most sensitive data in encrypted form. We use a range of technical and organizational practices to help protect the confidentiality, security, and integrity of the data on our systems, including SSL encryption compatible with major browsers.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Security</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We take reasonable organizational, technical, and administrative steps to protect your personal information. That said, no method of transmitting data over the internet or storing it electronically can be guaranteed 100% secure. Please avoid sending sensitive information by email. If you believe your account or interaction with us may have been compromised, please contact us right away using the details in the Contact section below.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Third Parties</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>This Privacy Policy covers Evo Meals only — we're not responsible for the privacy practices of third parties, including affiliates or any site linked from ours. A link to another site doesn't mean we endorse it.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Information About Services We Offer</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We want to provide the best possible service, so from time to time we may send details of products, services, refunds, promotions, or campaigns we think may interest you, with your consent. If you'd prefer not to receive these, you can unsubscribe any time by emailing us or updating your account settings.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Privacy Policy Amendment</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy at any time by publishing the new version on our website.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Verifying, Updating and Amending Personal Information</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>You can update your personal information any time by logging into your account and visiting your account settings.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Contact</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>We welcome any comments, questions, or requests about how we use your information. For anything related to this Privacy Policy, you can reach us by email at <strong>info@evo360.tech</strong>, or at <strong>Farwaniya, Kuwait</strong>.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/sitefoot') %>

</body>
</html>
